{%- doc -%}
  Loading placeholder for the About hero. Figma "About us skeleton"
  7930:95738.

  Scoped to the hero band, for the same reason the home one is: the rest of the
  page is server-rendered text and images that should paint as they land.

  The card's photo is a CSS background, which fires no load event of its own -
  so there is no `:defined` hook here and this leans on skeleton.js clearing at
  `complete`, which is after background images have loaded too.
{%- enddoc -%}

<div class="about-hero-skeleton skeleton" data-skeleton aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="about-hero-skeleton_wrapper">
    <span class="skeleton_tile skeleton_tile--card about-hero-skeleton_wrapper_card"></span>
  </div>
</div>
